      "title": "Railway Wonders of the World: In Northern Africa (1935)",
      "url": "https://www.railwaywondersoftheworld.com/northern-africa.html",
      "finding": "Contemporary account of the Maghreb trunk and selected branches. Intermediate points are schematic, not traced alignments."
    },
    {
      "id": "sncft",
      "title": "SNCFT historical chronology",
      "url": "https://www.sncft.com.tn/en/the-sncft/history/",
      "finding": "Operator dates northern and southern Tunisian openings; Heidra to Kasserine opened in 1940 and is omitted from the prewar view."
    },
    {
      "id": "oncf",
      "title": "ONCF 2013 annual report, historical timeline",
      "url": "https://www.oncf.ma/content/download/2471/27285/file/RAPPORT-ANNUEL-ONCF-2013.pdf",
      "finding": "Timeline dates Casablanca-Rabat to 1925, Oujda-Bouarfa to 1931 and Benguerir-Safi to 1936."
    },
    {
      "id": "nile35",
      "title": "Railway Wonders of the World: In the Nile Valley (1935)",
      "url": "https://www.railwaywondersoftheworld.com/nile_valley.html",
      "finding": "Contemporary Egyptian network account. Cairo-Aswan and Alexandria-Cairo are represented as schematic corridors."
    },
    {
      "id": "uk39",
      "title": "British official history: Mediterranean and Middle East I, chapter IV",
      "url": "https://www.ibiblio.org/hyperwar/UN/UK/UK-Med-I/UK-Med-I-4.html",
      "finding": "Pages 67-68 document road and single-track railway supply to Matruh at the outbreak of war. Water supply constrained railway operations."
    },
    {
      "id": "nwa42",
      "title": "US Army: Northwest Africa, chapter II",
      "url": "https://www.ibiblio.org/hyperwar/USA/USA-MTO-NWA/USA-MTO-NWA-2.html",
      "finding": "Pages 18-20 describe the 1942 road system, inland links and railways. Some roads had recent military improvements; this is not proof of 1939 condition."
    },
    {
      "id": "luce37",
      "title": "Milan civic historical collections: Pariani papers",
      "url": "https://www2.comune.milano.it/documents/462956031/464298261/Archivio_della_Guerra_Fondi_personali_II.pdf/68990940-5650-8265-1a70-4e6587006e00",
      "finding": "Archive catalog identifies March 1937 coastal-road inauguration documents at Bardia, Arae Philenorum and Misurata. Catalog evidence, not surveyed road geometry."
    },
    {
      "id": "w41",
      "title": "Wavell dispatch: operations December 1940-February 1941",
      "url": "https://www.ibiblio.org/hyperwar/UN/UK/LondonGazette/37628.pdf",
      "finding": "Dispatch identifies Benghazi railway junction and terminals at Barce and Soluch. This review establishes 1941 existence only."
    },
    {
      "id": "uk40",
      "title": "British official history: Mediterranean and Middle East I, chapter VI",
      "url": "https://www.ibiblio.org/hyperwar/UN/UK/UK-Med-I/UK-Med-I-6.html",
      "finding": "The 1940 account distinguishes the coast road from desert tracks, including Trigh Capuzzo. Road and track are separate classes."
    }
